  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1129 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nThursday, the next big upper level trough is expected \nto dig down the west coast. While staying under the ridge for the \nmean time, high temperatures are expected to be above average again \njust like Wed. However, the approaching system should bring back a \ntighter surface gradient and increase surface winds back to the 15-\n20 mph range. This next system is expected to bring cooler \ntemperatures back starting Friday with afternoon highs progged to be \na few degrees cooler. The current signal is that PoPs will be \nreturning to the Panhandles once again Thu night. However, there is \nstill some uncertainty to the potential rain amounts and best timing \nfor showers/storms Friday into the weekend. With 30 to 60 PoPs \nprogged through much of the weekend, increased cloud cover will \npotentially hold afternoon highs back in the 60s. PoPs are tapering \noff late Sunday into Monday but some 20-30 PoPs are holding on for \nnow, until the system speed is fully known.",
